{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:5cbd9acd762dc718","name":"GY-I Information Analysis Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-5cbd9acd762dc718","title":"GY-I Information Analysis Droid","revision":21043,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:03:15Z","sha256":"554e45ffd58f92a8b06eae3788508325b4d36f3b32056370bea6e7b31d432c52","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21043","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=GY-I%20Information%20Analysis%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-5cbd9acd762dc718","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scavenger's Guide to Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["An old adage says that credits make the galaxy turn. The truth of the matter is that those credits are often used to buy information. Originally, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybot Galactica"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybot_Galactica","referenceId":"reference:8d89ff519236e3e2"}," built the GY-I Information Analysis Droids to process the large amounts of data collected by space survey teams and university researchers. For example, a GY-I might be tasked with determining the best habitat on a newly discovered planet. However, as Emperor Palpatine turned resources away from the explorations of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"}," to the war machine of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},", most GY-I Droids were reassigned to other roles in which their analysis would be useful.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["GY-I Information Analysis Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["The Sad Tale of GY-133"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["These Droids are in high demand in many markets. Criminals want them to run numbers. Corporations want them to find new sources of profit. Warlords want them to analyze flaws in plans of attack. High-end processors in the model's brain means the manufacturing corporation keeps clear records on who it sells the Droids to. The processors are a big reason we make tidy profit when we get one. A smart tech can turn a GY-I into a lot of different kinds of Droids- protocol, astromech, assassin. They don't stay on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sandcrawler"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sandcrawler","referenceId":"reference:79940a5d4b9f0ebf"}," for long."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Yes, advanced processors can be used for many things, but sometimes the Droid can be modified too well. The deep space scout modifications can be full of quirks. Uncle Tukka told about GY-133, a Droid on a 10-year scout mission with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zabrak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zabrak","referenceId":"reference:c2636ff18986b258"}," company. The Droid came back the only survivor. It went too long between ",{"tag":"a","children":["Memory Wipes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Memory_Wipes"},", and its personality matrix destabilized. The Droid thought it was the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zabrak"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zabrak","referenceId":"reference:c2636ff18986b258"}," scout who had been its owner. Could not understand why its family didn't recognize it, or why the wife had a new husband. Could not handle the difference between the memories it possessed and the reality it faced. GY-133 began stalking and eliminating the family, one by one..."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["-",{"tag":"a","children":["Klikk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Klikk?action=edit&redlink=1"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Playing a GY-I Information Analysis Droid"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Cautious is the best word to describe GY-I Droids in the field. The more data they can acquire, the more contingencies they can plan for. The Droids aren't good at adapting on the fly, and the random nature of emotional behavior is a mystery to them. They are, however, excellent at long-term planning. What might seem like luck or the intervention of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," to someone else is merely the result of proper analysis and planning to a GY-I Droid.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although playing a cautious character might seem inappropriate in the fast-action ",{"tag":"i","children":["Star Wars"]}," setting, these Droids definitely have their place. For example, they plan the big heists or the lightning-fast raids on Imperial strongholds. Selections from the Noble's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Leadership Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Leadership_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:a51a0918ead13923"}," are a great way to emulate the Droid's ability to make large groups operate well, and a few choices from the Scoundrel's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortune Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortune_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:5bd9c10b1af0ad71"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Misfortune Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Misfortune_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:572da85689e76d52"}," can make lucky breaks seem like they were part of the plan all along.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Modification: Astromech Droid"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The GY-I Information Analysis Droid is surprisingly robust in the field. Many Droids are reduced to scrap metal by the first glancing blow in combat, but because the GY-I is meant to store information worth salvaging, its processors are housed in a torso tough enough to survive the rigors of space travel. Pilots have discovered that a GY-I can even be modified to replace an Astromech Droid.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["First, reprogram the Droid's analysis module, which requires a DC 25 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check and 1 hour of work. This step essentially gives the Droid an astromech buffer with a stored number of jumps equal to the Droid's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," score. Next, detach the Droid's limbs, leaving only its torso and head, and fit the Droid into the astromech slot of a ship. This process requires a DC 30 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check and 2 hours of work. Finally, attach the Droid directly to the ship's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," with a DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check and a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Modification: Financial Wizard"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Although the impressive processing power of the GY-I is generally used for scientific or academic pursuits, elements on the galactic fringe have found different applications for these Droids. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Zorba the Hutt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Zorba_the_Hutt?action=edit&redlink=1"}," received a GY-I as part of a collection on a bad debt and tweaked the Droid to suit his purposes. By analyzing the efficiency of the crime lord's operations, the Droid could streamline procedures, identify areas of waste, and deduce who was skimming credits off the top. The Droid also had a knack for ruthlessly determining when a loan should be collected with prejudice. Had the GY-I not mysteriously disappeared, it could have become the first Droid lieutenant of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hutt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hutt","referenceId":"reference:38066b70aa2676d9"}," crime family.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["To modify a GY-I into a Financial Wizard, replace the Droid's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heuristic Processor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heuristic_Processor","referenceId":"reference:0c5e1a481742e09b"}," with that of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree"}," Battle Droid. This step requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check with a DC equal to the Droid's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},". Once the new processor is installed, the Droid can overcome its life-preservation directives and look solely at the bottom line of a situation. If the Droid's owner has the ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Wealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wealth"}]}," Talent, provided that the Droid has been involved in its master's finances, the master is treated as being two levels higher than he or she is for the purposes of determining how many credits the master gains from the ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Wealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wealth"}]}," Talent when gaining a level. An individual can only benefit from one Droid modified in such a way. The Droid can also make a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knowledge (Bureaucracy)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knowledge_(Bureaucracy)"}," check to assess the street value of any items presented to it or to its owner. \n"]},"\n","\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["GY-I Information Analysis Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n","Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["3rd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3rd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 1\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +6; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 5 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 13 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 10, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 15\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 18, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 